# The Haven's leaders: the chair at the stronghold and the council heads at the safehouses.
# Voice: warm, worried, practical, darkly funny sideways. The List is said sideways, never announced.

conv haven.leader.bear
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
topic "Ask about the bear on the door."
prio flavour
voice haven

node start
  say "Day two. The teacher's eleven slept in the gym, and somebody painted a bear on the doors so nobody would shoot through them."
  say "Nobody did. So now every house with children has one."
  > @eye "Why is one eye stitched shut?" -> eye
  > @mine "Could I have one painted?" -> mine
  > @other "Something else." -> hub

node eye
  say "Somebody touched it up with the wrong brush and nobody had the heart to start again. It has a patch on its belly too."
  say "It's been through more than most of us. Leave it be."
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node mine
  say? tier:haven>=trusted :: "You've a ribbon, haven't you. That does the same job. People see it and put the rifle down."
  say "It goes on doors, love, not on people. People get shot at anyway."
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

conv haven.leader.list
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when !exiled
topic "Ask about the names on the list."
prio world
voice haven

node start
  say "Every house keeps one. Who's here, who's moved on, who's gone to a better house."
  say "It's a list. You count people so you know when one's missing."
  > @crossed "Some names are crossed out." -> press
  > @drop "Fair enough." -> hub

node press
  say "Some are. People leave. People move to houses with more room."
  > @why "Who crosses them out?" -> told | half | shut   check persuade haven 2 easier:merciful harder:paranoid bg:elder,nurse
  > @let "Let it go." -> hub

node told
  say "Whoever's on the pencil that week. Some names go because the person went. Some go because the stores did."
  say "I didn't say that. Eat something before you go."
  do learn:haven.list
  > @thanks "Thank you for telling me." -> hub

node half
  say "The council does. The council has its reasons, and its reasons have names too."
  say "Ask me again when I know you better."
  > @later "Another time, then." -> hub

node shut
  say "That's the council's book, not mine. Ask the council. They'll say the same."
  > @fine "Something else, then." -> hub

conv haven.leader.supper
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
topic "Ask who they read out at supper."
prio flavour
voice haven

node start
  say "Before anyone eats, somebody reads a name. One of ours who's gone. Then the bowls go round, counted twice."
  say? kin :: "We read one of yours, once. That's why there's always a bowl for you."
  say "It's not much of a ceremony. It's what we've got."
  > @stay "Can I stay for it?" -> stay
  > @count "Why count the bowls twice?" -> count
  > @other3 "Something else." -> hub

node stay
  say "Anyone can stay. Sit at the end, keep your hat off, and don't eat before the name."
  > @back3 "I'll remember." -> hub

node count
  say "Once to see how many we've got. Once to see how many we are. If the numbers don't match, somebody goes without."
  say "Usually me. Don't tell the children."
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub
